WEBVTT

00:07.007 --> 00:10.010
[computer] Round 13.
Three minutes remaining.

00:21.688 --> 00:23.023
[Usagi yelps]

00:24.149 --> 00:25.567
I don't want you.

00:29.821 --> 00:30.780
[Usagi gasps]

00:33.241 --> 00:34.367
[grunts and gasps]

00:39.372 --> 00:40.707
[panting]

00:48.506 --> 00:49.632
[yells]

00:59.392 --> 01:01.019
[Usagi wheezing]

01:02.687 --> 01:04.355
[groaning]

01:10.820 --> 01:12.155
[screams]

01:39.390 --> 01:40.308
Damn it!

01:44.813 --> 01:48.149
[computer] There are two players
remaining until checkmate.

01:49.275 --> 01:50.527
[Queen grunts]

01:51.194 --> 01:52.946
- [Kota] Miss?
- [Usagi panting]

01:57.659 --> 01:58.868
[gasps]

02:01.830 --> 02:04.082
[Queen] Nobody cared
about saving that kid.

02:04.833 --> 02:07.877
When given the option,
they sided with the Queen.

02:11.131 --> 02:14.676
They'll do whatever it takes not to die.
It's a fact.

02:15.885 --> 02:19.180
Nobody wants to see a child be killed.

02:19.264 --> 02:22.642
But in the end,
everyone wants to save their own skin.

02:22.725 --> 02:25.103
Each and every human being is that way.

02:26.980 --> 02:28.898
[gasping] Then I guess…

02:31.359 --> 02:33.236
you've never met somebody

02:34.821 --> 02:36.573
that you really cared about.

02:43.663 --> 02:47.375
Fucking hypocrites like you
make me wanna throw up.

02:50.461 --> 02:51.504
[Usagi gasps]

02:51.588 --> 02:55.008
[Queen] If you really cared
about this kid so much,

02:56.009 --> 02:57.635
you'd die with him.

02:59.137 --> 03:02.348
But something tells me
you'll change your mind soon.

03:03.391 --> 03:04.601
You will.

03:05.810 --> 03:07.103
[cries out]

03:18.406 --> 03:19.324
Are you okay?

03:22.118 --> 03:23.077
I promise

03:24.871 --> 03:27.040
I won't stop protecting you.

03:28.583 --> 03:30.043
[siren blares]

03:30.126 --> 03:33.671
[computer] Round 14.
Challenger Team's turn beginning.

03:34.255 --> 03:37.008
- This turn will last five minutes.
- [gasps]

03:37.967 --> 03:40.470
- Turn, start.
- [bell rings]

03:46.851 --> 03:48.853
[theme music]

04:54.210 --> 04:55.586
- Usagi!
- [gasps]

04:55.670 --> 04:57.046
Stay where you are!

05:02.302 --> 05:03.970
[whimpering]

05:04.512 --> 05:06.931
- You okay?
- [gasps] I have an idea.

05:07.015 --> 05:08.099
Follow me.

05:14.772 --> 05:15.815
[Arisu] Ow!

05:31.122 --> 05:32.874
- [panting]
- You all right?

05:33.416 --> 05:34.292
Did you see them?

05:34.375 --> 05:37.170
Okay, there isn't much time
left on the clock, so we have to--

05:37.253 --> 05:38.379
- [all yell]
- Run!

05:38.963 --> 05:40.715
[energy crackling]

05:41.632 --> 05:42.675
[yelling]

05:48.139 --> 05:50.224
Usagi. We need to capture five more.

05:50.308 --> 05:52.143
I saw people upstairs. Let's go!

05:52.226 --> 05:53.102
[Usagi] Wait!

05:53.603 --> 05:55.438
Let's go! Come on, Usagi.

05:55.521 --> 05:56.481
[Usagi] Wait.

06:04.238 --> 06:05.948
- [all panting]
- [Usagi] You guys…

06:07.033 --> 06:09.702
Do you really wanna
keep working for the Queen?

06:11.204 --> 06:12.747
Yeah, of course we do.

06:13.706 --> 06:14.874
We don't wanna die.

06:15.458 --> 06:18.086
If we keep playing for the Queen's side
and we win,

06:18.169 --> 06:19.712
then we can stay right here.

06:20.254 --> 06:23.216
If we're in this arena,
we don't need to play anything else.

06:23.841 --> 06:25.760
No getting hunted down or shot.

06:26.344 --> 06:29.722
You've gotta be kidding me.
Winning isn't the most important thing!

06:29.806 --> 06:31.808
[player 1] Right now? Yeah. Yeah, it is.

06:34.143 --> 06:35.895
No. You're wrong about that.

06:38.564 --> 06:39.607
Listen.

06:40.817 --> 06:44.904
The most important thing
isn't just winning the game!

06:47.949 --> 06:49.826
It's getting back to our world.

06:54.163 --> 06:56.416
If all you really care about is winning,

06:57.291 --> 06:59.377
then sure, you're doing everything right.

06:59.460 --> 07:03.631
You're protected by the Queen,
and you can live in this world forever.

07:06.175 --> 07:07.802
But is that what you want?

07:09.470 --> 07:12.098
If our side wins, we can beat the Queen.

07:12.181 --> 07:14.725
If we beat every single face card game,

07:15.726 --> 07:17.270
then there's a chance…

07:17.353 --> 07:19.480
a chance we can get back home again.

07:23.359 --> 07:26.237
[player 2] There's no going back there.
Ever.

07:27.738 --> 07:29.073
That world's all over.

07:30.658 --> 07:31.993
It's just over.

07:33.161 --> 07:35.621
These games have rules,
just like the rest.

07:36.956 --> 07:39.834
The face card guys,
if they lose, they get killed.

07:40.793 --> 07:42.003
Just like us.

07:42.086 --> 07:43.629
Which means if we beat them,

07:44.338 --> 07:46.007
then there won't be anyone else.

07:46.883 --> 07:49.427
This will all end
if we win every face card game.

07:50.428 --> 07:52.722
That's just a guess, man,
and nothing more.

07:53.848 --> 07:54.891
Yeah, a guess.

07:55.850 --> 07:56.726
And hope.

07:58.478 --> 08:00.563
Maybe hope is what we need to survive.

08:01.189 --> 08:02.398
I won't give up.

08:03.816 --> 08:06.777
[Usagi] Sure, you can extend
your lives here with the Queen.

08:07.570 --> 08:08.863
But what does that mean?

08:10.156 --> 08:13.826
Y-- you're spending the rest of your lives
killing each other.

08:17.663 --> 08:18.706
That's not a life.

08:21.876 --> 08:23.794
Why don't you take a chance with us?

08:29.634 --> 08:32.512
[player 3] This place
isn't that different from our world.

08:35.473 --> 08:37.850
You guys want to go back
to our world so badly?

08:39.977 --> 08:41.062
That place sucked.

08:42.980 --> 08:44.148
Maybe…

08:46.442 --> 08:48.152
Maybe this one'll be better.

08:59.413 --> 09:00.540
[Usagi] Yeah.

09:02.416 --> 09:04.126
I thought the same until recently.

09:06.170 --> 09:08.506
Going back might not be all that great.

09:12.969 --> 09:13.970
But you know…

09:16.472 --> 09:18.558
I want to go back, I really do.

09:23.437 --> 09:25.606
I wanna make it back to our world.

09:29.777 --> 09:31.988
For all the pain and heartache
I lived with,

09:34.448 --> 09:36.117
I was born and raised there.

09:38.452 --> 09:40.371
And it made me who I am today.

09:42.164 --> 09:43.499
I miss that world.

09:48.462 --> 09:50.590
At times, it was unbearably lonely.

09:55.094 --> 09:57.221
But I believe it taught me kindness.

09:58.681 --> 09:59.974
That life that I had…

10:01.517 --> 10:03.978
I'm kind here because it made me that way.

10:08.566 --> 10:10.985
This world makes kindness easy to forget.

10:19.201 --> 10:20.536
I want to return.

10:23.331 --> 10:25.291
I want to give that life another shot.

10:41.474 --> 10:42.433
[player 4] I…

10:44.101 --> 10:45.311
I wanna go back.

10:49.398 --> 10:50.316
I do.

10:52.109 --> 10:54.862
I want to return and see

10:56.238 --> 10:57.323
my family.

11:11.671 --> 11:13.673
[energy crackling]

11:15.716 --> 11:16.717
Do you think…

11:19.178 --> 11:20.388
Could I start over?

11:24.850 --> 11:27.603
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Two turns remaining.

11:27.687 --> 11:31.440
Round 15 is the final one
for the Queen Team.

11:31.524 --> 11:34.193
This turn will last five minutes.

11:34.777 --> 11:36.487
- Turn, start.
- [bell rings]

12:00.219 --> 12:01.220
[sighs]

12:02.430 --> 12:04.807
[Arisu] They have 14 on their side?

12:04.890 --> 12:07.435
We need to get back five people
for a majority.

12:07.518 --> 12:09.270
How do we do that in just one turn?

12:09.353 --> 12:11.564
The other side can win just by running.

12:11.647 --> 12:14.734
Okay, then.
We chase and catch them one by one.

12:15.651 --> 12:16.527
Wait.

12:22.575 --> 12:23.951
There's one more option.

12:24.034 --> 12:25.453
[dynamic music]

12:29.915 --> 12:33.043
[Queen] I want that guy on our side
before the game's over.

12:34.336 --> 12:35.546
And the woman?

12:38.632 --> 12:39.800
I don't want her.

12:41.427 --> 12:44.597
Let's teach her that fake virtues
have no place in this world.

12:46.766 --> 12:48.017
- Aah!
- Let's go!

12:53.606 --> 12:54.815
Come here!

12:58.194 --> 12:59.403
Stop running!

13:01.906 --> 13:03.866
Okay. Run!

13:15.336 --> 13:16.253
[player 1] Down there!

13:17.254 --> 13:18.547
[player 2] Stop running!

13:27.723 --> 13:29.850
- We don't need you. Move!
- [yells]

13:29.934 --> 13:30.976
[all gasping]

13:34.146 --> 13:35.231
[player 3] After her!

13:40.736 --> 13:42.321
- [Queen] This way!
- All right!

13:53.082 --> 13:54.208
You, upstairs!

13:54.708 --> 13:55.543
Run.

14:00.130 --> 14:01.298
[player 4] Over there!

14:03.551 --> 14:05.386
- Found him!
- [player 5 laughs]

14:06.053 --> 14:07.471
Woo-hoo!

14:07.555 --> 14:08.556
Faster!

14:15.396 --> 14:18.148
[all breathing heavily]

14:20.025 --> 14:21.151
[PA chimes]

14:21.235 --> 14:24.405
[computer] Round 15 is ending shortly.

14:24.488 --> 14:26.782
Thirty seconds remaining.

14:45.968 --> 14:47.344
Grab him!

14:47.428 --> 14:48.888
[Arisu yelling]

14:50.556 --> 14:51.640
[both yelling]

14:54.435 --> 14:56.770
[computer] Final turn, start.

14:57.688 --> 14:58.564
[Arisu yells] Go!

15:04.236 --> 15:05.154
[both yell]

15:05.237 --> 15:07.406
- Arisu!
- [yells]

15:11.076 --> 15:12.536
[player] They went that way!

15:15.039 --> 15:16.040
[yells]

15:18.000 --> 15:19.960
- Get him!
- [panting]

15:20.044 --> 15:21.378
- Oh! Oh!
- We did it! Yeah!

15:21.462 --> 15:23.505
- I can't believe it!
- Fuck, yeah!

15:45.527 --> 15:47.029
- Yeah!
- Yes!

15:47.112 --> 15:48.280
- [laughing]
- We won!

15:49.073 --> 15:50.741
- This is incredible!
- We won!

15:50.824 --> 15:52.743
[all talking and laughing]

15:53.494 --> 15:55.120
Yeah, we did so great!

15:55.788 --> 15:57.414
We pulled through!

15:57.498 --> 15:58.582
- Yes!
- We showed them!

15:58.666 --> 16:00.334
- We did it. We won.
- [player] Yes!

16:01.251 --> 16:03.087
- Oh yes!
- That was so bad!

16:03.170 --> 16:06.256
- We pulled through. You pulled through!
- No, you were great!

16:06.799 --> 16:09.593
- Great! Well done! Well done!
- Yes!

16:19.269 --> 16:22.106
[Queen] I don't know
how you convinced everyone.

16:23.273 --> 16:24.900
But congratulations,

16:24.984 --> 16:26.860
Miss Goody Two-Shoes.

16:28.904 --> 16:30.155
When I go back,

16:31.657 --> 16:33.367
I'm not going to be alone.

16:33.993 --> 16:35.661
I'm leaving with my friends.

16:37.121 --> 16:38.122
They matter.

16:38.622 --> 16:39.540
[scoffs]

16:40.332 --> 16:41.625
That's what you think?

16:43.877 --> 16:46.255
You have way more freedom here, you know.

16:47.631 --> 16:51.385
This place is much more my scene
than that rigid world.

16:52.511 --> 16:54.096
You were players, weren't you?

16:55.180 --> 16:57.808
You were brought here to play,
just like us.

16:57.891 --> 16:59.560
You had to play the games.

17:00.644 --> 17:01.812
Well, am I wrong?

17:05.315 --> 17:07.818
Oh, you'll find out soon enough.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.487
- Once the games are done.
- Not before then?

17:12.031 --> 17:14.033
What'll we learn when they're all over?

17:16.035 --> 17:18.495
First you clear all the face cards.

17:19.496 --> 17:21.123
Then you'll know everything.

17:22.416 --> 17:23.792
Will we learn where we are?

17:23.876 --> 17:25.961
Can we go back to our world?

17:29.131 --> 17:31.508
You'll have to wait and find out, baby.

17:33.052 --> 17:34.928
- [computer] Time is up.
- Hey!

17:35.429 --> 17:39.224
[computer] It is game over for everyone
on the Queen's Team.

17:41.018 --> 17:43.562
I wanna live free until my last breath.

17:44.813 --> 17:45.731
[Usagi gasps]

17:46.315 --> 17:47.441
See you later.

17:50.027 --> 17:50.944
[all gasp]

17:56.283 --> 17:58.327
[power whirring]

17:59.453 --> 18:00.871
[crackling]

18:26.438 --> 18:27.648
[Usagi sighs]

18:31.944 --> 18:33.654
[cicadas chirping]

18:37.366 --> 18:39.243
[Arisu] I want to finish these games.

18:40.702 --> 18:41.829
I want the answer.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.166
But more than that…

18:48.210 --> 18:50.129
I wanna go back to our world.

18:52.965 --> 18:54.341
Both of us together.

19:00.681 --> 19:01.682
So do I.

19:14.361 --> 19:15.362
Hey, look.

19:17.364 --> 19:19.366
[low rumbling]

19:23.787 --> 19:25.038
[Usagi sniffs]

19:25.122 --> 19:26.790
That smell…

19:29.084 --> 19:29.960
Did you fart?

19:30.752 --> 19:31.920
Of course not!

19:35.966 --> 19:38.051
[water rushing and bubbling]

19:43.140 --> 19:44.433
[Usagi gasps]

20:16.089 --> 20:17.174
Hot! [winces]

20:20.928 --> 20:21.929
Wow! [laughs]

20:22.596 --> 20:24.139
It's a hot spring!

20:24.223 --> 20:25.641
There's a hot spring!

20:26.600 --> 20:28.685
Usagi! Look!

20:28.769 --> 20:30.979
- It's really a hot spring!
- [Usagi] Oh…

20:31.855 --> 20:33.774
The water's perfect over here!

20:33.857 --> 20:36.068
Really? Then let's get in!

20:36.902 --> 20:39.905
When's the last time we took a bath?
We can't pass this up!

20:40.489 --> 20:42.324
- [Usagi] Huh? Together?
- Huh…

20:43.408 --> 20:45.285
Huh? Oh…

21:02.636 --> 21:03.804
[groans]

21:05.430 --> 21:07.975
I could die right now and I'd be happy.

21:08.809 --> 21:10.102
[Usagi exhales]

21:12.354 --> 21:13.689
I just wish that…

21:15.190 --> 21:17.693
the painful memories washed away
as easily as dirt.

21:20.612 --> 21:21.863
Yeah, I know.

21:25.158 --> 21:26.118
[Usagi yelps]

21:27.494 --> 21:28.537
What's wrong?

21:29.246 --> 21:30.247
Usagi?

21:32.541 --> 21:33.583
Usagi?

21:35.752 --> 21:36.712
Hey!

21:37.629 --> 21:38.880
Usagi?

21:43.010 --> 21:44.344
That's not possible.

21:46.346 --> 21:48.140
They can't be real, can they?

21:49.933 --> 21:51.351
[Usagi gasps]

22:04.281 --> 22:05.574
[snorts]

22:07.701 --> 22:09.244
They're taking a bath too.

22:11.830 --> 22:14.041
Maybe they escaped from a zoo
or something.

22:17.336 --> 22:19.004
If we hadn't been brought here,

22:20.339 --> 22:21.840
we'd have never seen this.

22:23.717 --> 22:24.593
Yeah.

22:28.013 --> 22:29.681
You know what's kind of crazy?

22:30.849 --> 22:32.642
I'm feeling emotional.

22:33.560 --> 22:35.771
And I'm not entirely sure why.

22:38.732 --> 22:39.775
[sighs]

22:40.400 --> 22:41.902
Right there with you.

22:57.125 --> 22:58.043
[gasps]

22:59.294 --> 23:01.630
I'm sorry. I didn't see anything!

23:01.713 --> 23:05.092
Just elephants! I'm only looking at them.

23:05.717 --> 23:07.260
I love elephants.

23:07.344 --> 23:08.553
It's okay.

23:11.014 --> 23:12.099
You can stay.

23:24.986 --> 23:26.113
[Usagi sighs]

23:40.544 --> 23:42.671
- [elephant trumpets]
- [Usagi gasps]

23:47.092 --> 23:48.260
[gasps]

24:57.996 --> 24:58.914
[gasps]

25:03.418 --> 25:04.669
[breathing shakily]

25:15.555 --> 25:16.932
[leaves rustling]

25:17.015 --> 25:18.225
[wind whistling]

25:34.074 --> 25:35.158
[sighs]

26:02.644 --> 26:03.687
Found it.

26:24.165 --> 26:26.751
KIMIKO KUINA
ADMITTED: JUNE 2, 2021

26:50.358 --> 26:51.985
Mom, I wanna see you again.

27:54.631 --> 27:55.924
[engine chugging]

27:56.007 --> 27:58.009
[faint radio chatter]

28:04.057 --> 28:05.934
[man] This makes me sick.

28:07.894 --> 28:10.105
All the work of some twisted fuck.

28:13.274 --> 28:15.985
[Ann] Stuff like this
makes me lose hope for humanity.

28:17.153 --> 28:19.280
[man] This person knew
they were gonna die.

28:20.448 --> 28:22.409
But they fought until the very end.

28:25.662 --> 28:27.122
They didn't give up hope.

28:50.603 --> 28:52.105
There's still hope here.

29:00.864 --> 29:02.866
[engine rumbling]

29:23.803 --> 29:28.016
SUPREME COURT

29:43.948 --> 29:45.158
[Chishiya] Fascinating.

29:46.534 --> 29:49.078
So you were the King of Diamonds
all along.

29:49.704 --> 29:51.664
The Beach executive.

29:51.748 --> 29:53.833
Former Number Two.

29:53.917 --> 29:55.293
Kuzuryu.

29:57.670 --> 30:00.882
Why was the King of Diamonds at the Beach?

30:03.426 --> 30:04.844
I was curious.

30:05.470 --> 30:07.096
Undercover, then.

30:07.931 --> 30:09.349
[computer chimes]

30:09.432 --> 30:12.101
Difficulty, King of Diamonds.

30:12.185 --> 30:15.188
Game, Beauty Contest.

30:17.774 --> 30:19.025
Let us begin.

30:19.108 --> 30:21.110
[tense music]

30:34.624 --> 30:37.961
[computer] Rules.
Contestants have three minutes

30:38.044 --> 30:41.422
to choose a number between zero and 100.

30:42.173 --> 30:47.470
The average of the numbers
everyone selected is multiplied by 0.8.

30:47.554 --> 30:52.183
The person who chose the number
closest to that result is the winner.

30:53.393 --> 30:58.648
Multiply the average value
of what we all chose by 0.8.

31:00.358 --> 31:03.778
Whoever's number
is closest to that result wins.

31:04.279 --> 31:05.280
Hmm?

31:05.363 --> 31:09.033
Multiply the average value by 0.8?

31:10.285 --> 31:13.246
Why 0.8? What's 0.8 mean?

31:14.414 --> 31:15.498
I get it.

31:16.541 --> 31:19.252
Multiplying the average
by the fixed value of 0.8

31:19.335 --> 31:21.004
disrupts the scale's balance.

31:22.422 --> 31:23.631
That's why it's a game.

31:24.841 --> 31:26.217
0.8 is a drop.

31:26.759 --> 31:29.220
A single drop straight from heaven.

31:30.847 --> 31:34.100
[computer] One point will be deducted
from the four losers,

31:34.183 --> 31:36.603
and the round is concluded.

31:36.686 --> 31:42.275
When a player reaches negative ten points,
they will receive a game over.

31:42.358 --> 31:45.904
The last player standing
will clear the game.

31:45.987 --> 31:51.326
However, every time a player
is eliminated, a new rule is added.

31:51.409 --> 31:54.287
A new rule? What's with that?

31:57.081 --> 31:59.792
And nobody's explaining these scales.

32:00.293 --> 32:03.880
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Round one, start.

32:17.852 --> 32:19.270
Hmm…

32:22.273 --> 32:23.149
[chimes]

32:25.902 --> 32:26.778
[chimes]

32:34.035 --> 32:34.911
[chimes]

32:42.126 --> 32:43.086
[chimes]

32:43.169 --> 32:45.880
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Time limit reached.

32:47.924 --> 32:51.219
The average of the numbers
chosen in the first round

32:51.928 --> 32:54.138
is 32.8.

32:54.764 --> 32:58.393
After multiplying this value by 0.8,

33:00.228 --> 33:02.438
the player closest to this number

33:02.522 --> 33:04.315
is Master Kuzuryu,

33:04.983 --> 33:06.025
the winner.

33:12.448 --> 33:14.742
[player] If everyone picked 40,

33:16.077 --> 33:17.954
then the average value

33:18.037 --> 33:19.998
would be 40, of course.

33:20.081 --> 33:22.750
Multiplying that by 0.8 is 32.

33:22.834 --> 33:25.545
Even if everyone anticipated that
and chose 32,

33:25.628 --> 33:29.132
multiplying the average value by 0.8
will yield a lower number.

33:29.215 --> 33:30.967
So that won't work.

33:31.050 --> 33:33.636
If everyone picks the same, that means

33:34.762 --> 33:37.306
getting stuck in a cycle and no one wins.

33:37.974 --> 33:40.393
[grunts] So we can't do that. Nah.

33:40.476 --> 33:42.437
Ah, I understand.

33:42.520 --> 33:46.691
You just need to predict your opponents'
moves and be a few steps ahead.

33:46.774 --> 33:50.111
Mmm… This feels like a heart
more than a diamond.

33:50.862 --> 33:52.697
Hmm! We're reading each other.

33:52.780 --> 33:55.199
Whether you play poker or chess,

33:55.283 --> 33:58.619
in an intellectual game,
you have to read your opponent.

33:59.996 --> 34:01.414
Not reading their minds,

34:02.123 --> 34:03.916
but predicting their reasoning.

34:04.751 --> 34:06.044
Wouldn't you say?

34:08.337 --> 34:09.756
Huh, King?

34:11.382 --> 34:12.550
Their reasoning?

34:19.515 --> 34:20.892
You ignoring me?

34:20.975 --> 34:22.769
[liquid pouring]

34:23.561 --> 34:24.562
What's that?

34:25.313 --> 34:26.355
Water?

34:29.233 --> 34:31.319
[Kuzuryu] That is sulfuric acid.

34:31.402 --> 34:34.530
- [woman] What?
- [Chishiya] Oh, so you'll answer him…

34:35.865 --> 34:38.868
[man] If someone reaches
negative ten points, the scales will tip.

34:40.411 --> 34:42.038
[Kuzuryu] It'll melt our bodies.

34:43.456 --> 34:45.833
Best case, we end up horribly disfigured.

34:52.090 --> 34:53.382
Scales, well…

34:54.884 --> 34:56.427
Let me guess.

34:56.511 --> 34:58.471
The King of Diamonds is a lawyer.

34:58.554 --> 35:00.348
At least, he used to be.

35:02.266 --> 35:04.018
Yes, but that's in the past.

35:04.602 --> 35:05.812
That bad, was it?

35:06.854 --> 35:09.941
But even so, you selected this venue.

35:11.692 --> 35:14.779
Interesting game arena, the Supreme Court.

35:16.155 --> 35:18.241
This giant installation.

35:18.324 --> 35:21.744
The badge a lawyer wears
represents equality and fairness.

35:21.828 --> 35:25.581
All life, including yours,
is equally valuable.

35:26.499 --> 35:28.459
Is that what you wanna say?

35:28.543 --> 35:30.336
What you want us to understand?

35:30.419 --> 35:31.420
[laughs]

35:32.672 --> 35:36.843
The scale will always tip
to whatever side has more gold.

35:38.594 --> 35:40.346
Not all life has the same value, you know.

35:43.683 --> 35:44.725
[buzzer sounds]

35:44.809 --> 35:47.395
[computer] Round two, start.

35:48.104 --> 35:50.565
[thinking] Since 26 was the answer before,

35:50.648 --> 35:53.359
maybe I'll multiply that by 0.8 this time?

35:53.985 --> 35:56.904
No, everyone might be
thinking the same thing.

35:56.988 --> 35:59.657
Ah, maybe I'll multiply it by another 0.8?

36:00.616 --> 36:02.785
[man thinking]
Suppose everyone chooses 100.

36:02.869 --> 36:05.788
The product after multiplying it by 0.8
would be 80.

36:05.872 --> 36:09.375
In order to win, picking a number
higher than 80 is pointless.

36:09.458 --> 36:13.880
If 80 is the highest average we can have,
multiplying it by 0.8 is 64.

36:14.589 --> 36:18.968
If the highest average is 64,
then multiplying that by 0.8 is 51.2.

36:19.051 --> 36:20.178
So 51.

36:20.887 --> 36:23.848
And we can go on and on,
getting closer and closer to zero.

36:24.348 --> 36:26.350
The law of the stock market is to invest

36:26.434 --> 36:28.644
in stocks that
everyone wants to invest in.

36:29.437 --> 36:31.981
You have to predict everyone's desires.

36:32.064 --> 36:34.692
[thinking] The crux of this game
is to read a few steps ahead

36:34.775 --> 36:36.652
of everyone else's deductions.

36:37.278 --> 36:41.824
There are already equations that exist
to help read an opponent's rationality.

36:41.908 --> 36:44.327
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Time limit reached.

36:44.869 --> 36:48.623
The average of the numbers
chosen in the second round

36:48.706 --> 36:51.167
is 16.6.

36:51.250 --> 36:54.879
After multiplying this value by 0.8,

36:56.047 --> 36:58.424
the player closest to this number

36:59.300 --> 37:02.470
is Master Kuzuryu, the winner.

37:03.512 --> 37:05.181
[acid pouring]

37:05.264 --> 37:06.599
[sighs]

37:16.484 --> 37:18.611
You were even closer this time.

37:19.570 --> 37:22.448
[thinking] The number is getting smaller.

37:22.531 --> 37:24.617
So, what, we're supposed to pick zero?

37:26.786 --> 37:29.205
[thinking] The rational conclusion
would be zero.

37:29.705 --> 37:32.375
In other words,
everyone will pick zero in the end.

37:34.669 --> 37:37.546
[thinking] Picking zero
is the most rational choice.

37:37.630 --> 37:41.509
But the rational limit
is different for everyone.

37:44.971 --> 37:46.097
Kuzuryu.

37:47.765 --> 37:48.599
[Kuzuryu] What?

37:49.725 --> 37:51.352
I think I understand now.

37:52.478 --> 37:54.480
The thing that you're trying to measure…

37:56.774 --> 37:58.442
it's the value of life, isn't it?

38:00.319 --> 38:01.404
[exhales]

38:02.196 --> 38:03.239
No, it's not.

38:04.115 --> 38:05.533
Then what are you doing?

38:06.742 --> 38:07.868
You can tell me.

38:20.298 --> 38:23.217
[Kuzuryu] Perhaps we could propose
a new settlement figure?

38:23.718 --> 38:27.930
The contaminants that the factory dumped
actually did cause environmental issues.

38:28.014 --> 38:31.142
Twenty people in the surrounding community
died as a result.

38:31.225 --> 38:33.477
[man] Diseases can be caused
by many factors.

38:34.312 --> 38:36.897
What proof is there
that our company is responsible?

38:39.817 --> 38:42.320
I heard that you were
an extremely talented lawyer,

38:42.403 --> 38:44.947
but it seems
you do not understand the law.

38:45.573 --> 38:49.160
Laws don't exist
to protect the weak from the powerful.

38:49.785 --> 38:51.996
Everyone is equal
in the eyes of the law, sir.

38:52.079 --> 38:53.247
[man] That is naive.

38:56.417 --> 38:58.836
In order to save starving people,

38:58.919 --> 39:02.381
you first need the power
to influence the world's economy.

39:03.007 --> 39:07.011
Your principles are not enough to change
a world so full of contradictions.

39:07.762 --> 39:08.763
Let me ask you.

39:11.140 --> 39:15.936
What do you think we should do
to maintain a respectable, modern society?

39:19.065 --> 39:20.608
We need a justice system.

39:20.691 --> 39:23.652
A fair justice system
must exist at all levels.

39:24.820 --> 39:25.863
You mentioned…

39:26.364 --> 39:29.867
You mentioned the importance
of respecting the world's economy.

39:30.493 --> 39:33.412
But prioritizing economic growth
will create more inequality.

39:33.496 --> 39:34.705
- A wealth gap--
- No!

39:35.539 --> 39:39.335
Your duty as a lawyer
isn't to make sound arguments.

39:39.418 --> 39:41.712
Any fool is able to preach equality.

39:42.380 --> 39:46.884
Fairness and justice have no place
in a world more full of monsters than men.

39:46.967 --> 39:47.927
[sighs]

39:48.010 --> 39:51.389
[man] However, thanks to the power
of human imagination,

39:51.472 --> 39:54.266
we can make an unfair argument
sound fair and just.

39:54.975 --> 39:56.936
And you will do just that.

39:57.019 --> 39:59.772
It is your solemn duty
that is given to you by God.

40:09.407 --> 40:11.784
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Time limit reached.

40:11.867 --> 40:14.370
The results of the third round.

40:17.498 --> 40:18.707
[player in striped shirt] 100?

40:18.791 --> 40:21.794
[computer]
The average of the numbers is 20.2.

40:21.877 --> 40:24.839
After multiplying this value by 0.8,

40:24.922 --> 40:28.592
the player closest to this number
is Master Daimon, the winner.

40:28.676 --> 40:30.344
[gasps] Huh? I won?

40:30.428 --> 40:31.387
I won?

40:31.887 --> 40:32.721
Ah! Yes!

40:33.347 --> 40:34.432
What's up, man?

40:35.558 --> 40:36.809
Why'd you do that?

40:37.476 --> 40:40.104
You picked 100.
That means you'll always lose.

40:40.187 --> 40:43.107
There's a zero percent chance of winning,
don't you know?

40:43.983 --> 40:46.902
I think all of you are overthinking this.

40:48.362 --> 40:50.781
That kind of stuff
just gives me a headache.

40:51.866 --> 40:53.367
So I blew it up.

40:53.451 --> 40:54.660
[pulsing music]

40:54.743 --> 40:56.454
[acid pouring]

41:01.333 --> 41:02.251
[scoffs]

41:03.085 --> 41:04.753
[laughs] Wow, you're insane.

41:05.671 --> 41:06.839
[chuckles]

41:07.423 --> 41:09.133
[buzzer sounds]

41:09.717 --> 41:13.512
[computer] The winner of round six
is Master Chishiya.

41:20.227 --> 41:22.855
The winner of round seven is…

41:22.938 --> 41:23.981
[tune plays]

41:24.064 --> 41:25.483
…Master Daimon.

41:28.777 --> 41:30.779
[shrieks] Oh yeah!

41:30.863 --> 41:31.739
[laughs]

41:38.829 --> 41:41.707
I definitely don't wanna die like that.

41:43.751 --> 41:45.377
[buzzer sounds]

41:45.461 --> 41:47.671
[thinking] I'm at minus nine points.

41:47.755 --> 41:49.882
If I miss any more, I die.

41:50.382 --> 41:52.510
My formula must be foolproof.

41:57.097 --> 42:01.310
[thinking] What do I do? I'm so lost here.
I can't use the same strategy.

42:02.311 --> 42:04.396
[thinking] I can't make a single mistake.

42:04.897 --> 42:06.815
The next time I lose, it's game over.

42:08.192 --> 42:10.110
[thinking] Rationally speaking,

42:10.861 --> 42:13.697
the average
should be getting closer to zero.

42:16.951 --> 42:19.078
[Chishiya]
I bet he predicted this outcome.

42:22.915 --> 42:24.375
[chiming]

42:24.458 --> 42:25.459
[groans]

42:29.588 --> 42:30.422
[chimes]

42:30.506 --> 42:32.967
[computer] The winner of round ten is…

42:33.050 --> 42:33.884
[tune plays]

42:33.968 --> 42:36.178
…Master Kuzuryu.

42:37.846 --> 42:39.265
[chiming]

42:39.348 --> 42:42.893
[computer] Two players
now have negative ten points.

42:42.977 --> 42:44.019
[man whimpering]

42:48.232 --> 42:51.777
[computer] It is game over
for these participants.

42:52.444 --> 42:53.445
[acid pouring]

42:55.489 --> 42:56.657
[acid hissing]

42:57.241 --> 42:59.451
[screaming]

42:59.535 --> 43:03.122
Take this off! Someone!
I'll do anything! [screams]

43:03.956 --> 43:08.502
Don't! Ah! Take this off!
Hey! Take this off!

43:08.586 --> 43:09.628
What do you want, huh?

43:10.212 --> 43:12.047
You want money? Please!

43:12.131 --> 43:14.300
[whimpers] What can I do?

43:14.383 --> 43:15.593
[gasping]

43:15.676 --> 43:18.178
Please, stop this! Just stop!

43:18.262 --> 43:20.264
[screaming]

43:27.229 --> 43:28.897
[yelping]

43:36.697 --> 43:38.324
[metal creaking]

43:40.826 --> 43:41.744
[whimpering]

43:41.827 --> 43:43.996
[screaming]

43:58.427 --> 44:00.429
[screaming]

44:04.016 --> 44:05.309
[groaning]

44:07.102 --> 44:09.188
- [thump]
- [shrieks]

44:11.023 --> 44:13.442
Now, this is more like a face card game.

44:13.525 --> 44:14.818
[sizzling]

44:14.902 --> 44:17.321
[Chishiya]
Is this the equality you're after?

44:18.489 --> 44:19.406
[chiming]

44:19.490 --> 44:22.034
[computer] As two players were eliminated,

44:22.117 --> 44:24.745
two new rules will be added.

44:24.828 --> 44:26.246
Rule number one.

44:26.330 --> 44:29.249
If two or more players choose
the same number,

44:29.333 --> 44:33.295
they will be disqualified from the round
and will each lose one point.

44:33.379 --> 44:34.963
Rule number two.

44:35.047 --> 44:36.924
Choosing the exact correct number

44:37.007 --> 44:41.261
will cause the other players
to lose two points instead of one.

44:48.060 --> 44:49.561
[sighs]

44:50.229 --> 44:52.231
[breathing shakily]

44:53.857 --> 44:55.067
[gasps]

44:55.818 --> 44:56.694
[chimes]

45:00.364 --> 45:01.407
[chimes]

45:03.617 --> 45:04.743
[chimes]

45:07.037 --> 45:08.038
[buzzer sounds]

45:08.122 --> 45:10.666
[computer] Results for round 11.

45:16.046 --> 45:18.090
All of us picked zero?

45:18.173 --> 45:23.303
All three players picked the same number
and are disqualified from the round.

45:23.387 --> 45:25.764
All three players lose one point.

45:25.848 --> 45:27.057
Huh?

45:27.141 --> 45:29.518
Everyone ended up
choosing the same number.

45:31.061 --> 45:35.023
[thinking] If that happens one more time,
it's game over for me.

45:36.734 --> 45:39.528
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Round 12, start.

45:40.154 --> 45:41.029
[chimes]

45:43.949 --> 45:44.992
[chimes]

45:48.287 --> 45:49.580
[chimes]

45:50.164 --> 45:52.583
[computer] Results for round 12.

46:01.383 --> 46:02.342
[tune plays]

46:02.426 --> 46:05.637
[computer] As the winner chose
the exact correct number,

46:06.305 --> 46:09.475
the other two players
will lose two points.

46:12.060 --> 46:13.103
[Daimon] No way.

46:13.187 --> 46:15.939
No way! This can't be happening!
How did you…

46:17.483 --> 46:19.401
You saw my answer, didn't you?

46:19.485 --> 46:21.236
He cheated! He did!

46:21.320 --> 46:24.656
You did! How else would you be able
to know which number I chose?

46:24.740 --> 46:26.950
I knew it because I've been watching.

46:27.785 --> 46:31.413
At the start of the last round,
you had negative eight points,

46:31.997 --> 46:33.707
and I had negative nine.

46:34.416 --> 46:37.795
Even if you lost,
you'd still get another chance.

46:37.878 --> 46:40.672
So you took a risk,
thinking we'd eliminate each other.

46:40.756 --> 46:44.468
I thought about that,
and I figured you'd pick a random number.

46:44.551 --> 46:47.429
[scoffs] You want us to believe
you just guessed?

46:47.513 --> 46:48.430
Impossible!

46:48.514 --> 46:50.265
I knew what you thought we'd pick.

46:50.349 --> 46:52.893
Odds are we'd choose numbers under 50.

46:54.520 --> 46:56.814
[thinking] It's like he read my mind.

46:57.648 --> 47:01.235
The King was up by three points before.

47:09.409 --> 47:12.412
I couldn't catch up
if we chose the same number.

47:17.751 --> 47:22.089
But I still had a chance if I could
get them to pick the same number.

47:27.302 --> 47:30.013
[Chishiya] So you'd have to avoid
numbers under 50.

47:30.681 --> 47:32.724
And if you were going to do that,

47:32.808 --> 47:35.519
you'd have to avoid them
by a large margin.

47:36.103 --> 47:40.941
Even so, you wouldn't pick too high.
Ninety and up is too much.

47:41.024 --> 47:42.651
So over 50, under 90.

47:42.734 --> 47:46.113
When you ask people to guess a number,
a few things come to mind.

47:46.196 --> 47:48.073
Double digits, so they're out.

47:48.782 --> 47:52.452
Same thing with nice, round numbers
divisible by ten.

47:52.536 --> 47:56.039
When you put someone on the spot
and ask them to choose a number,

47:56.123 --> 47:58.417
they'll usually go for eights,
threes and fives,

47:58.500 --> 48:00.544
and some of those are prime.

48:00.627 --> 48:02.170
You'd try not to pick them.

48:02.254 --> 48:04.214
Not too many options left now.

48:04.965 --> 48:06.884
How do we narrow the list further?

48:06.967 --> 48:09.386
Some of these numbers we see every day.

48:09.887 --> 48:11.221
Game systems,

48:11.847 --> 48:13.432
movie titles,

48:13.515 --> 48:14.850
brand logos.

48:15.350 --> 48:16.977
Easy associations.

48:17.060 --> 48:20.814
By my count, that just leaves 62 and 74.

48:20.898 --> 48:22.649
No way to narrow it down.

48:23.859 --> 48:25.527
So I… Well,

48:26.570 --> 48:27.946
I got lucky.

48:29.489 --> 48:32.784
[unsteadily] I knew
I shouldn't have picked 74.

48:33.285 --> 48:34.494
[chiming]

48:34.578 --> 48:38.290
[computer]
A player now has negative ten points.

48:41.209 --> 48:43.962
No, no. No. No, no!

48:44.046 --> 48:45.631
No! No, no!

48:45.714 --> 48:46.798
Don't!

48:46.882 --> 48:48.050
Please! Just let me go.

48:48.133 --> 48:50.218
I'll do anything! Let me go! Let me go!

48:50.302 --> 48:51.803
[wails] No!

48:53.013 --> 48:54.056
[screaming]

49:01.813 --> 49:03.815
[sizzling]

49:07.611 --> 49:08.570
Well…

49:10.364 --> 49:13.158
She said that not all lives

49:13.867 --> 49:15.369
have the same value.

49:17.371 --> 49:19.122
Think she still believed it?

49:19.873 --> 49:21.750
Up until the bitter end?

49:26.046 --> 49:27.089
[Kuzuryu] Tell me…

49:28.632 --> 49:32.344
Have you ever peered behind the curtain,
seen how the world really works?

49:35.097 --> 49:39.434
Watched children die because their parents
couldn't afford a few yen for medicine?

49:41.061 --> 49:44.481
Seen girls sold off
to pay for their parents' debts?

49:46.984 --> 49:50.404
Been powerless
to break the cycle of poverty?

49:53.198 --> 49:54.282
[buzzer sounds]

49:54.366 --> 49:57.244
[computer] A new rule is being added.

49:58.453 --> 50:02.040
If a player chooses zero as their number,

50:02.124 --> 50:06.003
the other player will win
if they choose 100.

50:07.671 --> 50:09.006
[Chishiya] A-ha.

50:09.798 --> 50:12.801
Since there's only two players
left in the game at this point,

50:13.593 --> 50:15.721
the one who picks closer to zero

50:15.804 --> 50:18.140
is inevitably going to be the winner.

50:18.974 --> 50:20.225
Just math.

50:20.308 --> 50:25.522
So if you pick zero each time, you'll win.
You're further from negative ten.

50:25.605 --> 50:27.899
But this new rule changes everything.

50:28.525 --> 50:29.901
I still have a chance.

50:30.986 --> 50:32.946
If you choose zero,

50:33.030 --> 50:35.198
I can win by choosing 100.

50:37.117 --> 50:39.828
But then if you think I'll choose 100,

50:41.496 --> 50:44.041
you can choose one, and you'll win.

50:45.792 --> 50:47.419
Three choices.

50:47.502 --> 50:50.255
It all comes down to three choices.

50:50.338 --> 50:53.091
Zero, one, and 100.

50:53.175 --> 50:55.969
Rock, paper, scissors.

51:00.766 --> 51:02.976
But I've only got one point left.

51:03.060 --> 51:06.104
If we tie,
that's game over for me, isn't it?

51:08.732 --> 51:10.901
The stakes couldn't be higher
if you tried.

51:13.111 --> 51:14.279
[buzzer sounds]

51:15.113 --> 51:16.031
I get it.

51:16.823 --> 51:19.618
You're desperately trying
to make this fair.

51:20.577 --> 51:22.329
But why? Why bother?

51:25.707 --> 51:27.000
[Kuzuryu] Hypothetically,

51:27.834 --> 51:31.004
if there were a million doses
of a vaccine for a disease,

51:32.631 --> 51:34.841
which million people would you save?

51:37.302 --> 51:38.762
[Chishiya] Ahhh.

51:39.429 --> 51:40.806
I see it now.

51:42.599 --> 51:46.812
You don't wanna have to choose
who gets to live and who has to die.

51:48.105 --> 51:50.982
You don't want to determine
the value of a life.

51:51.858 --> 51:52.943
[Kuzuryu] Exactly.

51:53.902 --> 51:56.029
How could I weigh all the variables?

51:56.822 --> 51:59.699
What makes one life worth saving

51:59.783 --> 52:01.243
and one worthless?

52:02.869 --> 52:04.037
How can I know?

52:06.915 --> 52:07.833
So,

52:08.875 --> 52:10.335
tell me what you think.

52:12.087 --> 52:15.048
If you had to answer
the question put before you…

52:16.758 --> 52:17.926
What I'd do?

52:18.009 --> 52:20.178
Give 'em to kids with no parents or money.

52:22.931 --> 52:23.932
You would?

52:24.015 --> 52:25.517
I would try to do that.

52:26.268 --> 52:28.645
But I wouldn't be the one to choose.

52:28.728 --> 52:29.896
It's about money.

52:30.564 --> 52:33.692
Because anyone with enough money
can choose a life's value.

52:34.943 --> 52:37.445
I bet you've seen it. Am I right?

52:38.155 --> 52:39.823
You've peered behind the curtain.

52:39.906 --> 52:40.949
I have.

52:41.908 --> 52:44.536
After an accident,
there was no settlement paid out.

52:45.328 --> 52:48.373
People died when they couldn't afford
the proper treatment.

52:48.456 --> 52:50.292
So you understand.

52:51.293 --> 52:53.837
Why do you bother
striving for justice at all?

52:53.920 --> 52:55.046
Because I must.

52:57.382 --> 52:59.301
Equality is something we fight for.

53:14.566 --> 53:15.942
[beeping]

53:24.367 --> 53:26.995
[Chishiya] Very good. You were great.

53:27.954 --> 53:29.623
Next week is the big day.

53:30.248 --> 53:31.541
You keep it up, okay?

53:34.544 --> 53:35.462
Yeah.

53:37.589 --> 53:39.049
[crying] Thank you.

53:40.634 --> 53:43.053
[sobs] Doctor, thank you so much.

53:43.136 --> 53:44.846
- [Chishiya] Of course.
- [sobs]

53:46.264 --> 53:48.016
- [Chishiya] Excuse me.
- Yes, yes.

53:59.527 --> 54:01.905
[Chishiya] Hayato's condition
is finally stable.

54:01.988 --> 54:05.158
And that means this next surgery
should save his life.

54:05.242 --> 54:07.077
[doctor] Yes. About the surgery…

54:07.744 --> 54:08.870
Listen.

54:08.954 --> 54:11.623
There's been a change
to the transplant priority list.

54:11.706 --> 54:13.917
- You've made a change?
- [doctor] Yes.

54:18.630 --> 54:20.840
This patient was just moved up the list.

54:25.178 --> 54:28.390
The grandchild
of a good friend of the director's.

54:28.473 --> 54:30.892
- And what about Hayato?
- [doctor] Postponed.

54:31.810 --> 54:33.311
They're important.

54:34.771 --> 54:36.940
Their support keeps the hospital running.

54:40.151 --> 54:41.486
We don't have a choice.

54:42.237 --> 54:44.406
Medicine is all about this sort of thing.

54:46.074 --> 54:48.201
Now, go inform the patient's parents.

54:49.703 --> 54:51.121
But what do I say?

54:52.414 --> 54:53.415
[scoffs]

54:54.624 --> 54:57.752
You'll think of something.
He's your patient.

55:06.428 --> 55:07.971
[crying]

55:08.054 --> 55:09.389
Hayato…

55:21.151 --> 55:22.319
[doctor] Well…

55:22.402 --> 55:24.779
Even if he got the transplant last week,

55:24.863 --> 55:27.115
there was a chance
he wasn't going to make it.

55:31.036 --> 55:32.370
This isn't my fault.

55:33.413 --> 55:37.208
You should know by now
your ideals aren't enough to save a life.

55:43.131 --> 55:44.382
That's clear.

55:46.593 --> 55:48.845
I'm not gonna carry it with me, sir.

55:51.639 --> 55:52.807
This is our job.

56:10.033 --> 56:11.826
SAKURAZAKA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

56:18.083 --> 56:21.002
PHYSICIAN
PEDIATRIC CARDIOVASCULAR SURGERY

56:25.673 --> 56:27.133
[sighs]

56:27.217 --> 56:29.344
[doctor] So, take care of it.

56:29.427 --> 56:30.345
Sir.

56:44.067 --> 56:45.568
How fascinating.

56:48.279 --> 56:50.657
Perhaps I was brought to this place

56:51.366 --> 56:53.701
so I could play this game with you.

56:59.457 --> 57:01.376
I'm going to choose 100.

57:07.215 --> 57:08.425
Why would you say that?

57:09.467 --> 57:11.136
Just giving you some help.

57:12.679 --> 57:13.805
Are you mad?

57:14.681 --> 57:16.808
You can't just tell me what you'll choose.

57:16.891 --> 57:20.103
Unless I select zero this round,
you've guaranteed your death.

57:24.190 --> 57:25.692
Sitting across from you

57:26.818 --> 57:29.237
is a man who is charging towards death.

57:30.905 --> 57:32.115
You have to decide.

57:33.032 --> 57:34.868
What value does this life hold?

57:36.161 --> 57:37.745
What value does my life hold?

58:23.041 --> 58:25.126
It's huge. Why bother?

58:28.046 --> 58:30.465
[man] We lost everything
when we came here.

58:35.553 --> 58:37.680
To abandon our ideals would be mad.

58:46.564 --> 58:47.690
Ideals?

58:50.193 --> 58:52.195
[echoing gasps and shouts]

59:06.668 --> 59:07.877
[man] Hey. Come on.

59:07.961 --> 59:11.714
[Kuzuryu gasping]
What are you doing? Just go.

59:11.798 --> 59:12.924
[man] I can't do that.

59:13.716 --> 59:17.095
In the last game I played,
a young man saved my life.

59:17.929 --> 59:20.848
Now it's my turn to save someone.
I have to pay it forward.

59:23.268 --> 59:24.852
You're not getting left behind.

59:25.478 --> 59:27.146
I'm choosing to fight for this.

59:27.230 --> 59:28.982
- [gasps]
- [echoing shouts]

59:30.984 --> 59:32.110
You're choosing?

59:34.487 --> 59:35.530
Now let's go.

59:58.261 --> 59:59.512
[chimes]

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:02.515
[computer] Time limit reached.

01:00:02.599 --> 01:00:05.101
The winner of round 13 is…

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:06.811
[tune plays]

01:00:06.894 --> 01:00:08.730
…Master Chishiya.

01:00:14.319 --> 01:00:16.321
You actually selected zero?

01:00:25.330 --> 01:00:28.041
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Round 14, start.

01:00:32.337 --> 01:00:33.546
[chimes]

01:00:45.892 --> 01:00:49.771
[computer]
The winner of round 14 is Master Chishiya.

01:01:00.907 --> 01:01:04.160
[Chishiya] That's it then, isn't it?
Only one point left each.

01:01:04.243 --> 01:01:05.745
This is the last round.

01:01:10.750 --> 01:01:14.170
- [buzzer sounds]
- [computer] Round 15, start.

01:01:19.717 --> 01:01:20.760
[Chishiya] So, then,

01:01:21.719 --> 01:01:22.929
can you do it?

01:01:27.266 --> 01:01:29.686
If you're finding it hard
to make your choice,

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:31.729
you can just kill me.

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:34.440
That's fair, don't you think?

01:01:36.401 --> 01:01:38.403
[Kuzuryu] I cannot make that decision.

01:01:39.737 --> 01:01:42.907
Was that your aim the whole time,
Master Chishiya?

01:01:42.990 --> 01:01:45.410
To make sure
that our scores ended up tied?

01:01:47.495 --> 01:01:48.496
In a way.

01:01:50.248 --> 01:01:51.999
I wanted to witness this.

01:01:53.292 --> 01:01:55.962
I wanted to be around
for your final choice.

01:02:03.761 --> 01:02:04.887
[chimes]

01:02:12.270 --> 01:02:14.981
If you pick one, you win.

01:02:24.907 --> 01:02:27.493
- [crowd cheering]
- [house music playing]

01:02:28.661 --> 01:02:29.829
[Kuzuryu] Ms. Momoka.

01:02:32.290 --> 01:02:34.333
Would you answer a question for me?

01:02:36.627 --> 01:02:38.087
You volunteered.

01:02:38.171 --> 01:02:39.839
Someone had to be the witch.

01:02:39.922 --> 01:02:41.549
But that means killing yourself.

01:02:47.889 --> 01:02:49.182
Why would you do that?

01:02:51.392 --> 01:02:52.769
I did it for my ideals.

01:02:57.774 --> 01:03:00.026
[Momoka] The human heart is
a beautiful thing.

01:03:02.153 --> 01:03:04.030
Human life is precious.

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.449
I believe that, truly.

01:03:09.702 --> 01:03:11.204
And when I look at my life,

01:03:12.079 --> 01:03:15.625
I know I've been able to survive
because of those ideals.

01:03:16.959 --> 01:03:18.294
[sounds fade]

01:03:19.045 --> 01:03:21.047
[gentle, poignant music]

01:03:21.672 --> 01:03:24.050
Your games and rules don't get to kill me.

01:03:26.594 --> 01:03:29.013
I'm not going to die because I lost.

01:03:31.808 --> 01:03:34.602
I'm doing this
to show you all that you're wrong.

01:03:35.978 --> 01:03:39.232
They're not going to kill each other
because they're not all bad.

01:03:46.948 --> 01:03:49.367
If I'm destined to die here someday…

01:03:51.744 --> 01:03:54.121
then I get to choose how I walk that path.

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:02.630
[Kuzuryu] I'm just one man.

01:04:04.423 --> 01:04:06.342
I don't know the value of a life.

01:04:07.009 --> 01:04:08.386
Or the meaning of one.

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:14.433
And I don't think I ever will.

01:04:15.726 --> 01:04:17.603
I'll never be the one to decide that.

01:04:21.858 --> 01:04:24.151
But there's one thing
I'm able to decide now.

01:04:43.546 --> 01:04:44.755
[chimes]

01:04:49.468 --> 01:04:52.138
[computer] The final round is over.

01:04:58.269 --> 01:04:59.896
So you made your choice.

01:05:01.480 --> 01:05:03.399
The value of a life can't be decided.

01:05:04.567 --> 01:05:05.860
Tell me why you did it.

01:05:11.657 --> 01:05:13.367
I did it for my ideals.

01:05:15.620 --> 01:05:17.330
[computer] The winner is

01:05:17.413 --> 01:05:18.998
Master Chishiya.

01:05:20.291 --> 01:05:22.293
[chiming]

01:05:22.376 --> 01:05:25.630
A player has reached negative ten points.

01:05:26.172 --> 01:05:29.175
It is game over for that player.

01:05:34.055 --> 01:05:36.557
It's nice to see
that you can actually smile.

01:05:37.975 --> 01:05:39.352
I'm finally free.

01:05:44.148 --> 01:05:46.025
I made my own choice.

01:05:48.069 --> 01:05:49.737
And based on my own ideals.

01:06:05.127 --> 01:06:06.545
It's all because of you.

01:06:20.017 --> 01:06:22.645
[woman] At last. It's our turn.

01:06:28.567 --> 01:06:29.485
What?

01:06:31.153 --> 01:06:32.571
That doesn't excite you?

01:06:36.117 --> 01:06:38.285
If I'm going to have a game to myself…

01:06:40.538 --> 01:06:41.998
I want it to be fair.

01:07:17.783 --> 01:07:19.535
You quit while you were ahead.

01:07:20.411 --> 01:07:22.663
I gave you the chance to make that choice.

01:07:24.957 --> 01:07:26.500
I'm so jealous of you.

01:07:30.755 --> 01:07:32.757
[machinery clanks and hisses]

01:07:37.344 --> 01:07:39.346
[sizzling]

01:07:53.569 --> 01:07:55.571
[sizzling fading]

01:08:04.663 --> 01:08:08.918
GAME CLEAR
CONGRATULATIONS

01:08:09.001 --> 01:08:11.003
[wind rustling through leaves]

01:08:46.413 --> 01:08:48.415
[fast ambient music]

01:09:07.601 --> 01:09:09.812
[Arisu] We've almost died
a thousand times.

01:09:10.896 --> 01:09:12.648
We could still die, any second.

01:09:16.110 --> 01:09:17.236
I don't believe it.

01:09:18.404 --> 01:09:20.823
It's a miracle we made it
as far as we have.

01:09:25.202 --> 01:09:27.288
If it was a miracle that got us here,

01:09:29.123 --> 01:09:31.083
let's take the opportunity and fight.

01:09:33.794 --> 01:09:34.795
Me and you.

01:09:37.464 --> 01:09:38.340
Yeah.

01:09:43.762 --> 01:09:45.764
[emotional music swells]

01:10:11.540 --> 01:10:13.000
I'm going to make it home.

01:11:04.134 --> 01:11:06.845
For the future. For the me of tomorrow.

01:11:14.144 --> 01:11:16.146
[theme music]
